 "nurion_pool": {
  "present": true,
  "rule": "Nurion label-level data (user decision 'Nurion', inv_nurion.py; DECISIONS 'Nurion \ucd94\ucd9c'): $MLT/dft/nurion.extxyz.gz (collect of every processed result tar; kinds nur_* = D1-target jobs, nur_x_* = every other job) is an input of every run. Inputs are complete only if it exists and results/N_report.json describes it (extxyz_bytes == file size); N_report complete (all 23 result tars) is recorded, not required (the pipeline N-gate decides when FT data may be built). Read once per data build as a stream: the gzip is decompressed front to back, frames are cut on their atom-count lines and parsed in chunks of 5,000 through a node-local ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} file by mlt_common.read_extxyz (no seek in the gzip: ase seeks per frame, quadratic); the stream is hashed: its sha256 must equal the one recorded for the fingerprint (else not ready: a collect replaced the file), and when N_report describes the file read (same bytes) the structure count must equal its n_structures (STOP otherwise); a Nurion structure keeps only numbers / positions / REF_forces / info d0_id after its row is built (memory). Read after D0G3, before G4 (FT-dedupe). Leakage tags = inv_nurion's (target rows: the reaction's rxn_ids / fold / dipole; molecules: the union over every D1 target using them; non-target jobs: rxn_ids '', folds = their core's T1 fold (none for D'' cores), dipoles = own dipole; D0 controls: d0_id + D0 class), so the C-2 rules are unchanged (FT_k / FT_LODO_d drop by tag OR targets(); test = all rxn_ids held out; FT-d0hold by d0_id). Validation (agent, recommended option): a Nurion row without rxn_ids whose job core ('<dipole>/<skeleton>' of $D1RUN/d1_manifest.csv = fold_core) is a validation core is a validation row, so whole validation cores stay out of training; other rows without rxn_ids train.",
